MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_001: Bull's-eyes all around! Incredible, Peter! You hit such\nsmall targets, and they're so far away!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_002: Haha. I guess.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_003: I just saw you hit a hundred targets out of a hundred.\nYou must be the best marksman in Dagda.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_004: So...why do the animals you hunt always manage to\nget away from you?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_005: Oh... That's... Well...
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_006: I've heard old man Caddock say, "That kid's useless\non a hunt."
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_007: Aren't you frustrated?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_008: When I'm shooting at something alive, I start to feel\nbad for it, and my aim goes way off.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_009: What if that rabbit has a mom or kids or maybe a\nwhole rabbit family?!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_010: If it doesn't make it back home, they'll be sad.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_011: You have a rich imagination and a soft heart. I think\nthose are both good qualities.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_012: But old man Caddock is just gonna keep making \nfun of you.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_013: Yeah, I don't like getting picked on.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_014: I'm frustrated for you. You're really quite amazing.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_015: I just think people should give you more credit for\nyour top-notch archery skills.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_016: Also...don't you shoot at people all the time on\nthe battlefield?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_017: Yeah, that's hard for me too. I get real queasy when\nthe battle's over.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_018: I think it would be better for everyone if your aim\nwere more consistent in every situation.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_019: I don't know why you're telling me all this...
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_020: But knowing that you think about me, that you care...\nthat's what really matters.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_021: Oh, that is NOT the point! It's clear that you need\nme by your side!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_022: B-b-b-by my side?! You?!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_023: You heard me! I'll make sure you train your aim until\nyou're not scared of hitting anything!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_024: Fight well, win easy. That's how it's done.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_025: Oh. Training. Got it.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_C_026: Alright, I'll figure out how to make this work. Let's\ndo it, Peter.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_001: Sorry to keep you waiting, Peter! I've got an idea!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_002: Uhm... What?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_003: I have a way of training you that will calm your\nnerves and fix your aim.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_004: Do you know the story of the man who took aim at\nan apple placed on top of his son's head?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_005: No... That sounds dangerous.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_006: I've only read about it, but apparently, the man was\nhaving trouble with his aim.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_007: But he focused his mind, let go of his distracting\nthoughts...and loosed the arrow.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_008: *gulp* How'd it turn out?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_009: The arrow flew straight and pierced the apple clean\nthrough. It was a magnificent shot!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_010: So I thought, "Peter should try this kind of training!"
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_011: Aim at a person with an apple on their head?!\nI don't wanna do that!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_012: No, that's a bit much. We'll use a doll instead.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_013: What? That's not a challenge. I can hit that, easy.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_014: OK. Go ahead, then.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_015: But just so you know, that doll was made for me by\nmy dead mother, and it's really important to me.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_016: Whaaat?! I can't shoot at that!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_017: You have to! It's a special training drill!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_018: Use a different doll! What are you gonna do if I\nhit it?!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_019: That's the training! Try NOT to hit it!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_020: Mmgh...
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_021: Hooo... A-apple... I just gotta hit the apple, and\neverything will be OK.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_022: Ah!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_023: I... I hit it.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_024: You hit...the doll.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_025: I, I ruined it! Your precious, important doll!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_026: I... I... I broke it! *sob*
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_027: Why are you crying, Peter?! It's my doll!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_028: That's exactly why I'm crying! I didn't want to\nbreak it!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_029: Tialla, you jerk! Why'd you make me do that?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_030: I did it for you! You were supposed to learn to aim\nand not be scared!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_031: But that doll is one of a kind! Don't use something\nso important!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_032: I didn't think you'd hit it! Not in a million years!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_033: I thought you'd be able to hit the apple—not the doll!\nYou're terrible, Peter! I give up!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_034: Tialla! Wait!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_B_035: Ahh, why did this have to happen?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_001: I got so many books! Can't believe I got such\nvaluable old editions.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_002: Well hello, little girl. You look like you're doing well\nfor yourself.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_003: Your books look like they're worth a lotta money.\nDon't resist, or you're gonna get hurt.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_004: Wh-what are you doing? Get lost!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_005: I'll hold her here. Grab a horse cart or somethin'!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_006: Aaah!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_007: Quiet! I'll just tie you up so you don't make a fuss...
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_008: Th-the rope! It broke? What the hell's goin' on?!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_009: Get your filthy paws off Tialla!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_010: Peter...
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_011: Little runt shot the rope...and missed the girl?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_012: No one can make a shot like that. It's dumb luck.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_013: Let's grab the books and head out!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_014: Gods damn it! The cart's stuck! He jammed the\nwheel with an arrow!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_015: Next one's going between your eyes. I'd suggest\nyou run.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_016: Aaah! Please don't kill us!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_017: Are...are they gone?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_018: Yeah. You're safe now.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_019: Thank you, Peter. You saved me and my books.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_020: I guess we debunked the theory about your aim\nfailing when you're targeting real people.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_021: My aim was good because I was protecting someone\nI care about. I couldn't afford to miss.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_022: I'm just glad you're OK.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_023: Someone you care about.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_024: You mean because I'm a friend, right? Peter, for me,\nyou're...
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_025: Tialla? Did you get hurt?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_026: N-no. I'm fine. But...why were you here?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_027: I mean, I'm glad you got here in time to help me, but\nhow did you find me?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_028: I'd been looking for you. I wanted to give you this.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_029: My doll!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_031: Ultand helped me. We fixed it. Sorta.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_032: I'm sorry about before, Tialla. I know you were only\ntrying to help me.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_033: Ah!
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_034: I'm the one who should apologize. And I promise I'll\ntake better care of this doll.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_035: You're a good person, Peter.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_036: You're just realizing that?
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_037: I know I'm not perfect, but I promise to always keep\nyou safe.
MID_SE_Tia_Pet_A_038: I'd expect nothing less.